# The shipped GF15 benchmark report is loaded as a package resource and its
# on-disk bytes are hashed twice: D4 binds the digest into the metric identity,
# and D5's reader verifies the copied report against it. Under `* text=auto`
# these bytes would be LF in the repository and CRLF in a Windows checkout, so
# the same commit would present two different digests on the two CI legs.
# Freeze them like the evidence archives they are packaged from.
blueearth_cst/experiment/data/** -text -whitespace

# Accepted GF15 method and verbatim review records carry byte-level digests.
dev/records/milestones/r12/gf15-alternative-estimator-review/** -text -whitespace
